API-30: close a project in EN_deleteproject even if EN_open failed

A failed EN_open leaves the report file open, with its error messages
still in the stdio buffer, and the network data allocated, but does not
set Openflag. EN_deleteproject called EN_close only when Openflag was
set, so it leaked the file handle and the memory, and the report stayed
empty until the program exited. EN_deleteproject now always calls
EN_close. After the CRASH-14 fix EN_close can safely be called twice,
which happens whenever a program closes a project before deleting it.

Requires: CRASH-14

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb, after CRASH-14:
    git apply API-30_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 4b31273..bd27ab3 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -66,9 +66,10 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_deleteproject(EN_Project p)
 */
 {
     if (p == NULL) return -1;
-    if (p->Openflag) {
-      EN_close(p);
-    }
+
+    // Close the project even if it is not open: a failed EN_open leaves
+    // the report file open and the network data allocated
+    EN_close(p);
     remove(p->TmpHydFname);
     remove(p->TmpOutFname);
     remove(p->TmpStatFname);
